    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/bafkreihwgheaedo7sudkcmj5ufcyvx44gwinaz7zn2g4vm47cahbt66v7i",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/bafkreihwgheaedo7sudkcmj5ufcyvx44gwinaz7zn2g4vm47cahbt66v7i",
      "alt": "Alexander Yue\n@Alezander9\nX.com\nCompaction is a mistake.\nWhen an agent's context fills up, tools like Codex and Claude Code compact it:\n1. The model prefills the entire session again\n2. It writes a summary of everything so far\n3. A new session starts from that summary\nI measured this on a real ~400k-token session with Opus 5.5:\n→ 38 s and $1.99 when the prompt cache has expired\n→ 29 s and $0.17 when it hasn't\nAnd the summary is lossy. The exact error message, the file path, the one number you needed is often gone.\nSo I do something new for Mainplane",
      "ratio": 0.7222,
      "handle": "timkellogg.me",
      "url": "https://bsky.app/profile/timkellogg.me/post/3mz3ocloz6k2i",
      "uri": "at://did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/app.bsky.feed.post/3mz3ocloz6k2i",
      "likeCount": 82
    },
    {
      "thumb": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_thumbnail/plain/did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/bafkreiezu35ntwytmvh6gbd4ygvwrfwizjg7ogprj7wr5nj56hqcuxvgim",
      "fullsize": "https://cdn.bsky.app/img/feed_fullsize/plain/did:plc:ckaz32jwl6t2cno6fmuw2nhn/bafkreiezu35ntwytmvh6gbd4ygvwrfwizjg7ogprj7wr5nj56hqcuxvgim",
      "alt": "Context retrieval works the other way around.\nMainplane keeps the full record of every session as a file. When the context fills up, a new session starts right away with one instruction:iYou are continuing session X. Retrieve key context from it as you go.\"\nThe agent searches the old session and copies the exact lines it needs, when it needs them.\nSame session, same model: 15 s and $0.10 to get back to work. It does not depend on a cache hit, and nothing is paraphrased.\nThis is the bitter lesson applied to agent memory. Don't hand-design what the model should remember. Give it the full record and good tools, and let it decide.\nMainplane is open source (MIT). Link in the first comment.",
